    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/7123/0/474458/889/animal-care-technician-tg1179": {
      "title": "Animal Care Technician",
      "description": "Animal Care Technician - TG1179 Register Login Back to search results Animal Care Technician - TG1179 We wish to recruit a grade 3 Animal Care Technician. You will be responsible for the cleaning and disinfection of animal housing, research laboratories/test rooms, research equipment and animal unit support facilities. You will assist the technical team with the maintenance of animal breeding programmes and recording environmental conditions of animal holding areas. You will also be responsible for undertaking laundry room duties, stock checking, stock and goods delivery duties and the safe disposal of waste. This job is physical and manual handling plays an important part of the job. You will be required to take part in the weekend cover rota, for which extra payment is provided. Informal enquiries can be made to the SMAU Technical Operations & Facilities Manager, email: smau@st-andrews.ac.uk . Employees of the University have access to a wide range of staff benefits including: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the S&LAS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 30 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship.  Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk . Closing Date: 16 October 2026 Interview Date: 6 November 2026 Please quote ref: TG1179SB Job Description: TG1179SB FPs.pdf SMAU Salary: £25,353 - £26,707 per annum Start: 18 November 2026 or as soon as possible thereafter Apply now Back to search results Animal Care Technician - TG1179 School/Unit: SMAU Posted: 21/09/2026 Closing date: 16/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/2274/0/475017/889/associate-lecturer-education-focused-in-systematic-theology-aoac2194xx": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer (Education Focused) in Systematic Theology",
      "description": "Associate Lecturer (Education Focused) in Systematic Theology - AOAC2194XX Register Login Back to search results Associate Lecturer (Education Focused) in Systematic Theology - AOAC2194XX We wish to appoint a fixed-term, 0.8 fte Associate Lecturer (Education Focused) in Systematic Theology within the School of Divinity. The position will be held from 1 January 2027 to 31 December 2028 . You will be a scholar with a growing international reputation in Divinity and a commitment to delivering high-quality teaching. The successful candidate will be expected to have a range of interests, to contribute to the research culture of the School, and to be capable of teaching the subject to students from a wide range of backgrounds. Candidates should hold a PhD in a cognate discipline. Excellent teaching skills are essential. An interest in promoting knowledge exchange is desireable. Informal enquiries can be directed to the Head of School, Professor William Tooman, at wt21@st-andrews.ac.uk or the deputy-Head of School, Professor Sabine Hyland, at sph@st-andrews.ac.uk . In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk. Closing date: 20 October 2026 Interview date: TBC Job description: AOAC2194XX FPs.pdf Ref no: AOAC2194XXRS School of Divinity Salary: Grade 6 / £38.784 pa pro rata Start date: 1 January 2027 Part time: 29 hours per week Fixed term: 2 years Apply now Back to search results Associate Lecturer (Education Focused) in Systematic Theology - AOAC2194XX School/Unit: School of Divinity Posted: 01/10/2026 Closing date: 20/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
