    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4911/0/475333/889/personal-assistant-to-the-director-of-development-cg4870": {
      "title": "Personal Assistant to the Director of Development",
      "description": "Personal Assistant to the Director of Development - CG4870 Register Login Back to search results Personal Assistant to the Director of Development - CG4870 The University of St\nAndrews was named the UK's top university in The Sunday Times Good\nUniversity Guide 2027 , reaffirming its position as one of the world's\nleading centres of learning, teaching and research. Through a global community\nof alumni, philanthropists and supporters, the Development Office secures the\nphilanthropic investment that enables St Andrews to transform lives through\neducation, research and innovation. This is an exciting\nopportunity to join the Development Office at a pivotal time as the University\nadvances its ambitious £300 million Making Waves campaign supporting\nscholarships, world-leading research, capital projects and sustainability\ninitiatives. We are seeking an\nexceptional Personal Assistant to provide high-level executive support to the\nDirector of Development. Working in a fast-paced and internationally focused\nenvironment, you will play a central role in ensuring the effective operation\nof the Director's Office, acting as a trusted coordinator across a wide range\nof strategic activities. This varied and rewarding\nrole will involve managing a complex schedule, coordinating senior-level\nmeetings and international travel, preparing high-quality briefing materials\nand correspondence, and supporting engagement with alumni, donors and senior stakeholders\naround the world. You will also provide line management and support to the\nDevelopment Assistant (US), helping to ensure the smooth delivery of\nadministrative support across the team. The successful candidate\nwill be highly organised, proactive and professional, with outstanding\ncommunication skills, exceptional judgement and the ability to manage competing\npriorities with discretion and confidence. This is a rare opportunity to work closely with a\nsenior leader at one of the world's leading universities and to contribute to a\nfundraising campaign that will shape the future of St Andrews for generations\nto come. St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Personal Assistant to the Director of Development\nincludes: Financial\n    contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of\n    the S&LAS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions A hybrid working\n    environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of\n    family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount\n    scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff\n    parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus\n    travel Subsidised\n    sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access\n    to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access\n    to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual\n    Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing Date: 23 October 2026 Interview Date: 2 November / 3 November Please quote ref: CG4870LS Job Description: CG4870LSFPs.pdf Development Salary: £32,080 - £37,694 per annum Start Date: 01 December or as soon as possible thereafter Apply now Back to search results Personal Assistant to the Director of Development - CG4870 School/Unit: Development Office Posted: 07/10/2026 Closing date: 23/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5509/0/474907/889/ref-programme-officer-ad2920": {
      "title": "REF Programme Officer",
      "description": "REF Programme Officer - AD2920 Register Login Back to search results REF Programme Officer - AD2920 The University of St Andrews is seeking to appoint a Research Excellence Framework (REF) Programme Officer to support delivery of the University's preparations for REF 2029. This is an exciting opportunity to play a central role in one of the most significant strategic activities undertaken by the University. Working as part of the central REF team within Research & Innovation Services (RIS), the postholder will coordinate key aspects of the University's REF programme, ensuring activity is effectively planned, monitored and delivered across Schools, Units of Assessment and professional services teams. The role will have a particular focus on delivery of the Strategy, People and Research Environment (SPRE) elements of the University's REF submission. This will involve working closely with academic and professional services colleagues to support evidence gathering, stakeholder engagement, narrative development, quality assurance and submission readiness. We are seeking a highly organised and collaborative individual with strong project management, communication and analytical skills. The successful candidate will be comfortable working with complex information, managing multiple priorities and building effective relationships across a wide range of internal stakeholders. This role offers an excellent opportunity to gain experience of institutional research strategy, research assessment and programme management within a highly successful research-intensive university. For further information and informal enquiries, please contact Jaclyn Suttie at jms53@st-andrews.ac.uk. In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews. Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing date: 23 October 2026 Interview date: TBC Job description: AD2920RS FPs.pdf Ref no: AD2920RS Research and Innovation Services Salary: Grade 6 / £38,784 - £46,049 pa Start date: As soon as possible Full time Fixed term: Until December 2028 Apply now Back to search results REF Programme Officer - AD2920 School/Unit: Research and Innovation Services Posted: 28/09/2026 Closing date: 23/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (BST) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate or a recruiter? Candidate Recruiter ⚡ by Freshworks 1"
