    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6680/0/475496/889/assistant-gardener": {
      "title": "Assistant Gardener",
      "description": "Assistant Gardener Register Login Back to search results Assistant Gardener We are looking to appoint a\nnew member to join our gardening service team based at the North Haugh Grounds\nDepartment. You\nwill work as part of an experienced team lead by the grounds Team leader and\nwork effectively within your team. You\nwill be responsible for the upkeep of fine lawns, herbaceous borders, open\ngrassland meadows, natural woodland and all general gardening maintenance. Experience\nin operating modern gardening equipment would be advantageous. Experience\nin Horticultural knowledge would be advantageous along with PA1 /PA6\nqualification You\nmust have excellent communication skills and a keen and helpful manner. The\nability to cope under pressure and the ability to demonstrate a flexible\napproach without supervision is essential. You\nmust have a sound knowledge of Health and Safety and machinery maintenance. This\ncould be the perfect opportunity for the right candidate to join our\nexperienced team. Informal enquiries can be directed to jjr3@st-andrews.ac.uk Employees of the University\nhave access to a wide range of staff benefits\nincluding: Annual leave of 30 days, plus 5 public holidays pro rata Financial contribution to relocation where applicable Membership of the S&LAS Pension Scheme with generous employer\n    contributions A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where\n    appropriate and a range of family friendly policies Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and\n    subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes\n    for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn\n    Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we\nare and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to\ncreating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our\nparticipation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan,\nCarer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. \nWe particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian,\nminority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled\npeople. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship.  Information on\nother visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk. Job Description: MC1188 FPs.pdf Closing Date:        30 October 2026 Interview\nDate:      9 November 2026 Estates Salary: £25,353 per annum Start date: 1 December 2026 Apply now Back to search results Assistant Gardener School/Unit: Estates Posted: 08/10/2026 Closing date: 30/10/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
