    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/4991/0/475334/889/development-assistant-research-cg1110mx": {
      "title": "Development Assistant (Research)",
      "description": "Development Assistant (Research) - CG1110MX Register Login Back to search results Development Assistant (Research) - CG1110MX The remit of the Development Office is to develop and strengthen the University's position at the forefront of teaching, learning and research by inspiring active participation, investment and loyalty to St Andrews. We do this through fundraising for key University priorities and developing mutually beneficial relations with over 71,000 alumni, friends and benefactors worldwide. We are seeking a well-organised and highly motivated individual to undertake prospect research in support of the University’s successful and well-established major giving and events programme. The Development Assistant (Research) will work closely with colleagues in the major giving, events and database teams to identify and provide high quality information on prospective major donors and supporters for cultivation events and briefings in advance of meetings. The role holder will also use several research tools to identify prospective new donors, including undertaking research into individuals in the UK, USA and across the world. Database work is required and training in the use of the Raiser’s Edge database will be provided. Careful attention to detail, discretion in handling confidential material and a good understanding of the importance of fundraising in the higher education sector are also essential. The role will sit within the Prospect Research team and report directly to the Development Officer (Research). It is primarily based at Walter Bower House, Eden Campus, with the flexibility of home working approximately 50% of contracted hours. Further information and informal enquiries may be directed to Clare Cameron-Mackintosh, email: clh21@st-andrews.ac.uk St Andrews offers more than just a place to work—it is a place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are committed to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their best. In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews. The package for the Development Assistant (Research) role includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the S&LAS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and servicesFree staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 30 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people who are currently underrepresented in professional posts at the University. In accordance with the new immigration rules, it is with regret that this role does not meet the current suitability requirements set by the UKVI to enable sponsorship of migrant workers.  The University encourages all interested candidates to apply regardless of nationality and all applications received are assessed against the essential and desirable criteria listed in the further particulars.  The successful candidate will have to demonstrate their right to work in the UK prior to commencing employment and where required, obtain the right to work in the UK without relying on University sponsorship.  Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk Closing Date: 1 November 2026                 Interview Date: W/C 9 November 2026 Please Quote Ref: CG1110MX CM Job Description: CG1110MX CM FPs.pdf Development Salary: Grade 3, £25,353 - £26,707 per annum, pro rata Hours: 21.75 hours per week, Part Time Start date: 1 December 2026 or as soon as possible thereafter Duration: 12 Months (Maternity Cover) Apply now Back to search results Development Assistant (Research) - CG1110MX School/Unit: Development Office Posted: 07/10/2026 Closing date: 01/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6242/0/475117/889/post-doctoral-research-fellow-ar3048": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Fellow - AR3048 Register Login Back to search results Post-doctoral Research Fellow - AR3048 Applications are sought for a committed Post-doctoral Research Fellow to work with Professor Blesson Varghese conducting research for the EPSRC funded National Edge AI Hub ( https://edgeaihub.co.uk ). The Hub is a £12M flagship investment and comprises 15 universities and over 75 industry partners. The primary duties will be to develop a personal research area in addressing systems-oriented challenges for building real-world machine learning systems for resource-limited environments, such as in edge computing, plan and deliver research, and accompanying software artefacts and publications, collaborate with the universities and partners to meet the objectives of the Hub, supervise research students as appropriate, and assist in the development of research proposals. The successful applicant will have (or be near to completion of) a PhD in Computer Science or cognate discipline with expertise in machine learning systems and algorithms suited for cloud-edge, mobile, or IoT settings. The post is available for 18 months starting 5 January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. St Andrews offers more than just a place to work—it is a place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are committed to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their best. In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews. The package for the Post-doctoral Research Fellow includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies supporting work life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 days annual leave plus 5 public holidays Further information and informal enquiries may be directed to Professor Blesson Varghese, email: blesson@st-andrews.ac.uk . At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing Date: 2 November 2026 Interview Date: 13 November 2026 Please quote ref: AR3048SB Job Description: AR3048SB FPs.pdf School of Computer Science Salary: £38,784 per annum Start: 5 January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter Fixed term for 18 months Apply now Back to search results Post-doctoral Research Fellow - AR3048 School/Unit: School of Computer Science Posted: 02/10/2026 Closing date: 02/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
