    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/2280/0/475415/889/director-of-communications-marketing-and-public-affairs-ad2924": {
      "title": "Director of Communications, Marketing & Public Affairs",
      "description": "Director of Communications, Marketing & Public Affairs - AD2924 Register Login Back to search results Director of Communications, Marketing & Public Affairs - AD2924 The University of St Andrews is seeking a visionary and\nexperienced public relations leader to serve as its Director of Communications,\nMarketing, and Public Affairs. This senior strategic role will be responsible\nfor shaping and delivering a high quality, and proactive communications,\nmarketing and public affairs service across the University, guiding St Andrews’\nvoice, reputation, and engagement across local, national, and global platforms.\nWith oversight of strategic communications, brand and\nmarketing, and community relations and political engagement, the successful\ncandidate will play a central role in presenting St Andrews’ values,\nachievements, and ambitions to a diverse range of audiences. They will\narticulate the University’s research and teaching credentials, its brand and\nits clearly differentiated market position, and they will also advise the\nsenior leadership team and provide guidance on reputational opportunity and\nrisk, and sector developments.\nThis is a rare opportunity to shape the narrative and public\nengagement of one of the world’s most historic, prestigious and forward-looking\nuniversities.\nThis role will be primarily based in St Andrews with an\nexpectation of on-site working. St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Director of Communications Marketing & Public Affairs includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous\n    employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial\n    homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and\n    services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to\n    Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on\n    degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities\n    including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice\n    scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people Closing Date: 30 November 2026 Please quote ref: AD2924LS Job Description: AD2924LSFPs.pdf Communications, Marketing & Public Affairs Salary: Grade 9/ Competitive Start Date: As soon as possible Apply now Back to search results Director of Communications, Marketing & Public Affairs - AD2924 School/Unit: Directorate of Corporate Communications Posted: 07/10/2026 Closing date: 30/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
