    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5160/0/475465/889/post-doctoral-research-associate-in-homogenous-catalysis-ar3348": {
      "title": "Post-doctoral Research Associate in Homogenous Catalysis",
      "description": "Post-doctoral Research Associate in Homogenous Catalysis - AR3348 Register Login Back to search results Post-doctoral Research Associate in Homogenous Catalysis - AR3348 Applications are invited for a 2-year Postdoctoral Research Associate position to work with Dr. Amit Kumar at the School of Chemistry, University of St. Andrews, on the topics of organometallic chemistry, homogeneous catalysis, and polymer chemistry. The project aims to develop new organometallic catalysts and methodologies for the synthesis and recycling of renewable plastics, in particular using the approach of dehydrogenation and hydrogenation reactions. This role is available on a fixed-term basis for 2 years (with a possibility of extension) and is available to start on the 1st Feb 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter. Hours of work are full-time (36.25 hours). Flexible working hours may be discussed. The principal duty of the post-holder will be to carry out research in the research group of Dr. Amit Kumar as well as: 1. To provide day-to-day technical assistance and guidance to undergraduate and PhD students within the group, and to provide direction in chemical research. 2. To take leadership in the day-to-day running of the laboratory and upkeep of equipment. 3. Carrying out experimental risk assessments and ensure that your research is carried out safely. Eligibility You will have a Ph.D. in chemistry with a proven track record in homogeneous catalysis, organic, and organometallic chemistry. Experience of working in polymer chemistry (e.g. polymer synthesis/characterisation) is desirable. Effective written and verbal communication skills, good time-management and the ability to work independently, yet within a collaborative environment, are essential. Further information and informal enquiries may be directed to Dr. Amit Kumar, email: ak336@st-andrews.ac.uk Tel: 01334 463411. In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing date: 31 December 2026 Interview date: Mid January 2027 (TBC) Job description: AR3348RS FPs.pdf Ref no: AR3348RS School of Chemistry Salary: Grade 6 / £38,784 - £42,254 pa Start date: 1 February 2027 Full time Fixed term: 2 years Apply now Back to search results Post-doctoral Research Associate in Homogenous Catalysis - AR3348 School/Unit: School of Chemistry Posted: 12/10/2026 Closing date: 31/12/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/3594/0/475696/889/clinical-senior-lecturer-clinical-lecturer-education-focused-ao2053": {
      "title": "Clinical Senior Lecturer / Clinical Lecturer (Education Focused)",
      "description": "Clinical Senior Lecturer / Clinical Lecturer (Education Focused) - AO2053 Register Login Back to search results Clinical Senior Lecturer / Clinical Lecturer (Education Focused) - AO2053 The School of Medicine wishes to appoint a new\nClinical Lecturer/s (Education Focused). Appointment at Senior Clinical\nLecturer may be possible, dependent on experience. It is envisaged that the\nsuccessful candidate will be embedded in the delivery of undergraduate medical\neducation at St Andrews, including the exciting new MBChB (ScotCOM). They will have access to potential future development opportunities within the\nSchool, and be involved in School education functions across years, aligned to\nan Education Focused Clinical Lecturer position. St Andrews School of Medicine is at a pivotal\ntime, delivering the innovative MBChB (ScotCOM), alongside a well-established\nBSc (Hons) and working in partnership with the University of Dundee in the\nco-delivery of the graduate entry programme, ScotGEM. It is at the forefront of\ncommunity based medical education and is known for high student satisfaction. The role holder/s will have significant\nopportunity to contribute to the leadership, design and delivery of MBChB\n(ScotCOM). This is a community orientated five-year programme, promoting\ngeneral-ism alongside secondary care exposure, ensuring to place patients at\nthe centre of the students’ learning. The inaugural cohort commenced in 2023,\nand will graduate in 2028, with a target of 55 students per academic year. Successful applicants will be engaged in the\ncreation of clinically orientated modules, ensuring a high quality experience,\nmeeting GMC accreditation requirements. They will work as part of a core team\nfocusing on MBChB (ScotCOM) and on delivering teaching excellence across the\nrange of undergraduate medical programmes. Role holders will work for the School between\ntwo and four days per week, with flexibility within FTE to facilitate clinical\nworking. We request candidates state preferred sessional commitment within their\napplication.  An additional 0.5FTE is\nalso available on a fixed-term basis for 12 months. Candidates should indicate in\ntheir cover letter if they wish to be considered for the fixed-term role, as\nwell as the open-ended vacancy. The candidate should be clinically qualified\nand can be from any clinical background for the posts, i.e. from any Secondary\nCare specialty or General Practice / Primary Care.  Candidates must be practising in a\nsubstantive clinical post to qualify for the Clinical salary scale. This will\nbe discussed at interview and prior to any offer of employment NHS\nFife clinical sessions may be available if required, and potential\nopportunities could be discussed where relevant. Excellent teaching skills and an interest in\npromoting knowledge exchange are essential. Informal enquiries can be directed to the\nDeputy Head of School (MBChB Programmes) and MBChB Programme Director; Dr\nRebecca Walmsley (ram29@st-andrews.ac.uk). St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Clinical Senior Lecturer / Clinical Lecturer\n(Education Focused) includes: Financial contribution to relocation\n    (subject to\n    eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous\n    employer contribution of 14.5% Membership of the NHS Pension may be\n    possible. A hybrid working environment, including partial\n    homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and\n    services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to\n    Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on\n    degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities\n    including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice\n    scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people Closing Date: 02 November 2026 Interview Date: 24 November 2026 Please quote ref: AO2053LS Job Description: AO2053LSFPs.pdf School of Medicine Salary: Consultant Scale, based on experience Part Time: 14.5 - 29 hours per week Apply now Back to search results Clinical Senior Lecturer / Clinical Lecturer (Education Focused) - AO2053 School/Unit: School of Medicine Posted: 13/10/2026 Closing date: 02/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6010/0/475769/889/research-technician-tg1321": {
      "title": "Research Technician",
      "description": "Research Technician - TG1321 Register Login Back to search results Research Technician - TG1321 Applications are sought for a committed Research Technician to maintain, develop and support a suite of highly specialised analytical facilities in the geochemistry laboratories in the School of Earth & Environmental Sciences at the University of St Andrews. The lab facilities include several mass spectrometers with peripherals, a LA-LIBS system, sample prep space, and a wet chemistry lab. The primary duties of the research technician will be to maintain and operate the instruments, undertake troubleshooting and repairs when required, develop and optimize analytical methods, manage purchase orders, train users and oversee safety protocols. We particularly seek an individual with strong expertise in plasma-source instruments - both solution and laser based - and associated clean sample preparation techniques to support the (LA-)ICP-MS (Agilent QQQ 8900 and Element 2) and MC-ICP-MS (Nu Plasma) instruments. Additional experience in gas-source mass spectrometry would be useful but is not required. The technician would be expected to help with maintaining the gas-source mass spectrometry facilities of the school as required. The successful applicant will have a PhD degree in Earth Sciences, Chemistry or Physics with expertise in analytical sciences. This is a permanent position, starting as soon as possible. Further details of the position can be obtained from Dr Eva Stueeken ( ees4@st-andrews.ac.uk ) or Dr Nick Gardiner ( nick.gardiner@st-andrews.ac.uk ) or Dr Luke Bridgestock ( ljb35@st-andrews.ac.uk ) St Andrews offers more than just a place to work—it is a place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are committed to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their best. In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews. The package for the Research Technician includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies supporting work life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 days annual leave plus 5 public holidays At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. This role is not eligible for visa sponsorship.  Information on other visa options is available at https://www.gov.uk/check-uk-visa or by contacting our HR Immigration Team on hrimmigration@st-andrews.ac.uk . Closing Date: 10 November 2026 Interview Date: 16 December 2026 Please quote ref: TG1321SB Job Description: TG1321SB FPs.pdf School of Earth and Environmental Sciences Salary: £38,784 - £46,049 per annum Start: As soon as possible Apply now Back to search results Research Technician - TG1321 School/Unit: School of Earth & Environmental Sciences Posted: 16/10/2026 Closing date: 10/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6650/0/475761/889/scientific-officer-ar2704cm": {
      "title": "Scientific Officer",
      "description": "Scientific Officer - AR2704CM Register Login Back to search results Scientific Officer - AR2704CM The School of Chemistry at the University of\nSt Andrews is seeking an experienced Scientific Officer with expertise in small\nmolecule crystallography to join its single-crystal diffraction facility. Working\nclosely with Dr David Cordes (X-ray Crystallographer) the postholder will use\nadvanced diffraction instrumentation to tackle challenging structural problems\nand help deliver high-quality structural solutions across a diverse range of\nresearch projects. You will work directly with researchers across the School,\nproviding specialist expertise and helping them make the most of the facility’s\ncapabilities. In addition, the postholder will become\nfamiliar with the School’s powder X-ray diffraction facilities, providing\nessential support for their effective operation. This is an exciting opportunity for an\nexperienced crystallographer who enjoys scientific problem-solving, advanced\ninstrumentation and collaborative research, and who would like to play a key\nrole in supporting an important resource for the School’s research activities.\nWe are looking for a collaborative scientist who will contribute to the\nSchool’s research environment and share our commitment to equality, diversity\nand inclusion. For an informal discussion about the role,\nplease contact Dr David Cordes at dbc21@st-andrews.ac.uk, or Professor Sharon\nAshbrook, Head of the School of Chemistry, at chem-hos@st-andrews.ac.uk. St Andrews offers more than just\na place to work—it is a place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion,\nand wellbeing, and we are committed to creating\na workplace\nwhere staff can thrive and perform at their best. In addition to the salary on\noffer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working\nat the University of St Andrews. The package for the Scientific Officer role\nincludes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject\n    to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with\n    a generous employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including\n    partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and\n    national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and\n    Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced\n    tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development\n    opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary\n    sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public\n    Holidays At St\nAndrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form\na core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair,\ninclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national\ndiversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the\nRace Equality Charter. We\nparticularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority\nethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people who are currently underrepresented in Scientific Officer roles at the\nUniversity. The University encourages all\ninterested candidates to apply, and all applications received are assessed\nagainst the essential and desirable criteria listed in the further\nparticulars.  The successful candidate will have to demonstrate their\nright to work in the UK prior to commencing employment and where required, the University can support with visa\nsponsorship. Closing Date: 11 November 2026 Interview Date: W/C  30 November 2026 Please Quote Ref: AR2704CM Job Description: AR2704CM FPs.pdf Chemistry Salary: Grade 6, £38,784 - £46,049 per annum Start Date: As soon as possible Duration: Permanent, Full Time Apply now Back to search results Scientific Officer - AR2704CM School/Unit: School of Chemistry Posted: 16/10/2026 Closing date: 11/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your