    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5162/0/475750/889/research-fellow-ar3356": {
      "title": "Research Fellow",
      "description": "Research Fellow - AR3356 Register Login Back to search results Research Fellow - AR3356 Applications are sought for a committed Post-doctoral Research Fellow to work with Dr Nicola Allison on a NERC-funded project entitled \"The impact of amorphous calcium carbonate precursor phases on CaCO 3 palaeoproxies\". The primary duties will be to identify the conditions under which amorphous calcium carbonates likely form in marine calcifiers and then to determine how formation, via an amorphous calcium carbonate (ACC) precursor, influences the palaeoproxy chemistry of calcite and aragonite. The successful applicant will conduct CaCO 3 precipitations to characterise the fluid environment required to form and convert ACC to aragonite and calcite in vitro under simulated organism calcification conditions. They will visualise ACC formation and transformation using transmission electron microscopy. They will analyse the trace element and isotope geochemistry of the mineral phases formed via an ACC precursor to refine palaeoproxy calibrations. The postholder will work closely with collaborators at the University of St Andrews, and the University of Edinburgh and will contribute to data analysis, publication of results, presentation at scientific conferences, and the supervision of student researchers where appropriate. The successful applicant will have (or be near to completion of) a PhD in earth, physical, chemical or biological sciences with expertise in mineral precipitation, trace element/isotope geochemistry or electron microscopy. The post is available for 42 months starting 4.1.27 or as soon as possible thereafter. For further information and informal enquiries, please contact Dr Nicola Allison at na9@st-andrews.ac.uk In addition to the salary on offer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St Andrews: Financial contribution to relocation (subject to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with a generous employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality Charter. We particularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing date: 13 November 2026 Interview date: w/c 7 December 2026 Job description: AR3356RS FPs.pdf Ref no: AR3356RS School of Earth & Environmental Science Salary: £38,784 - £42,254 pa Start date: 4 January 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter Full time Fixed term: Until 30 June 2030 Apply now Back to search results Research Fellow - AR3356 School/Unit: School of Earth & Environmental Sciences Posted: 16/10/2026 Closing date: 13/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
    },
    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/6154/0/475772/889/post-doctoral-research-fellow-in-climate-and-macroeconometrics-ar3355cm": {
      "title": "Post-Doctoral Research Fellow in Climate- and Macroeconometrics",
      "description": "Post-Doctoral Research Fellow in Climate- and Macroeconometrics - AR3355CM Register Login Back to search results Post-Doctoral Research Fellow in Climate- and Macroeconometrics - AR3355CM We invite applications for a Post-doctoral Research Fellow to work with\nDr Martin Bruns on a project Short-run Climate Change Effects: Evidence from\nStructural Vector Autoregression funded by the Leverhulme Trust. The\nproject examines the economic effects of climate-related shocks such as natural\ndisasters or weather extremes, at a monthly or quarterly frequency. To do so, a\nseries of both methodological time series econometrics studies and applied\nclimate-related studies will be conducted, partly in cooperation with the\nUniversity of East Anglia Climatic Research Unit (CRU), the European Central\nBank (ECB), and the German Institute for Economic Research (DIW Berlin). The primary duties will be to\n    construct a database of monthly climate shocks which can be readily used in a\n    structural vector autoregression to\n    implement novel time series econometrics methods in software packages such as\n    R, Matlab, and Python to liaise\n    with external partners such as the CRU, ECB, and DIW Berlin to engage\n    in the wider research activities as part of the macro cluster at the department\n    of economics at St Andrews Business School to\n    disseminate the project findings at international conferences and related\n    events to attend\n    both internal and external training events as well as professional development\n    opportunities The successful applicant will have (or be near to completion of) a PhD in\neconomics with expertise in time series econometrics and macro-econometrics,\nhandling of large datasets, and will have an interest in environmental\nsciences. Evidence of engagement with climate-related research as well as\nBayesian econometric methods is desirable. The post is available for 60 months starting March 1, 2027, or as soon as\npossible thereafter. For further information please contact Dr Martin Bruns: mb630@st-andrews.ac.uk St Andrews offers more than just\na place to work—it is a place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion,\nand wellbeing, and we are committed to creating\na workplace\nwhere staff can thrive and perform at their best. In addition to the salary on\noffer for this position, there are a wide range of benefits for staff working\nat the University of St Andrews. The package for the Post-Doctoral Research\nFellow role includes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject\n    to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with\n    a generous employer contribution of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including\n    partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and\n    national goods and services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and\n    Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced\n    tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access to training and development\n    opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary\n    sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public\n    Holidays At St\nAndrews, equality, diversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form\na core pillar of our University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair,\ninclusive and supportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national\ndiversity charters and awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the\nRace Equality Charter. We\nparticularly welcome applications from people from Black, Asian, minority\nethnic and minority religions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing Date: 15 December 2026 Interview Date: 26 Janaury 2027 Please Quote Ref: AR3355CM Job Description: AR3355CM FPs.pdf Business School (Economics) Salary: Grade 6, £38,784 per annum Start Date: 1 March 2027 Duration: Fixed Term until 31 December 2031 Apply now Back to search results Post-Doctoral Research Fellow in Climate- and Macroeconometrics - AR3355CM School/Unit: Business School Posted: 16/10/2026 Closing date: 15/12/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
