    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/5998/0/476276/889/research-development-manager-arts-and-humanities-ad2915": {
      "title": "Research Development Manager (Arts and Humanities)",
      "description": "Research Development Manager (Arts and Humanities) - AD2915 Register Login Back to search results Research Development Manager (Arts and Humanities) - AD2915 Do\nyou have experience of understanding and disseminating complex information,\nanalysing and working with data? Can you provide expertise and support in\nresearch funding schemes for an academic community?\nWe’re looking for a proactive Research Development Manager (Arts &\nHumanities) to support and implement the University’s Research and Innovation\nStrategy. In this pivotal role, you will provide professional services support\nto assist individual researchers and research groups in Arts & Humanities\nto understand and optimise funding calls, provide specialist advice on the\npresentation and content of proposals to ensure alignment with funding criteria\nand scheme objectives, and guide applicants in relation to research application\nprocedures. You will make key contributions to new initiatives designed to\nimprove service or success rates and be prepared to take the lead on some of\nthese. What You’ll Do: Support the development and delivery of\n    research development plans for funding growth, aligned to the disciplines,\n    schools and funders in your remit. Provide expert advice on proposal content to\n    ensure alignment with funding criteria, including scheme objectives, project\n    management, resource justification, and key policies (e.g. EDI, research\n    integrity), ensuring compliance with funder requirements, Work with the Head(s) of Research Development\n    to manage the preparation of larger or collaborative research bids,\n    collaborating closely with academic community. Make key contributions to new initiatives\n    designed to improve service or success rates and be prepared to take the lead\n    on some of these. What We’re Looking For: An individual who can\n    translate their funder insights and discipline knowledge into sustained\n    delivery plans and activity policies. Significant experience and\n    understanding of employing different approaches and supporting internal\n    capacity building to develop excellent, fundable research underpinned by\n    excellent service design. A proactive,\n    collaborative mindset with a strong commitment and proactive approach to\n    customer service. Why Join Us? Be part of a forward-thinking team driving meaningful change. Work in a vibrant, supportive environment where ideas thrive. Make a tangible difference in how research benefits society. St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Research Development Manager (Arts and Humanities) includes: Financial\n    contribution to relocation Membership\n    of the USS Pension Scheme with generous employer contributions of 14.5% A hybrid working\n    environment, including partial homeworking where appropriate and a range of\n    family friendly policies, supporting work-life balance Staff discount\n    scheme for local and national goods and services Free staff\n    parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to Work Schemes and subsidised local bus\n    travel Subsidised\n    sports membership, reduced tuition fees on degree programmes for staff, access\n    to training and development opportunities including LinkedIn Learning, access\n    to library facilities, salary sacrifice scheme 34 Days Annual\n    Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing Date: Friday 18 November 2026 Interview Date: To be confirmed Please quote ref: AD2915LS Job Description: AD2915LSFPs.pdf Research and Innovation Services Salary: £38,784 - £46,049 per annum Start Date : As soon as Possible Apply now Back to search results Research Development Manager (Arts and Humanities) - AD2915 School/Unit: Research and Innovation Services Posted: 26/10/2026 Closing date: 18/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs By clicking “Accept All Cookies”, you agree to the storing of cookies on your device to enhance site navigation, analyze site usage, and assist in our marketing efforts. View our privacy policy Cookies Settings Reject All Accept All Cookies Privacy Preference Center When you visit any website, it may store or retrieve information on your browser, mostly in the form of cookies. This information might be about you, your preferences or your device and is mostly used to make the site work as you expect it to. The information does not usually directly identify you, but it can give you a more personalized web experience. Because we respect your right to privacy, you can choose not to allow some types of cookies. Click on the different category headings to find out more and change our default settings. However, blocking some types of cookies may impact your experience of the site and the services we are able to offer. Allow All Manage Consent Preferences Strictly Necessary Services Always Active These Services are necessary for the website to function and cannot be switched off in our systems. They are usually only set in response to actions made by you which amount to a request for services, such as setting your privacy preferences, logging in or filling in forms. You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work. Functional Services Functional Services With these services, the website is able to provide advanced functionality and personalization. They may be set by us or by third parties whose services we use on our sites. If you do not allow these services, this website may not function properly. Back Button Cookie List Search Icon Filter Icon Clear checkbox label label Apply Cancel Consent Leg.Interest checkbox label label checkbox label label checkbox label label Reject All Confirm My Choices 1 Technical Support Today New Messages Technical Support Chatbot (with creds) a few seconds ago Welcome to Technical Support. Please could you let us know whether you're a candidate o