    "https://www.vacancies.st-andrews.ac.uk/Vacancies/W/1447/0/476312/889/head-of-development-services-and-deputy-director-ad2928": {
      "title": "Head of Development Services and Deputy Director",
      "description": "Head of Development Services and Deputy Director - AD2928 Register Login Back to search results Head of Development Services and Deputy Director - AD2928 The University of St Andrews was named the\nUK's top university in The Sunday Times Good University Guide 2027,\nreaffirming its position as one of the world's leading centres of learning,\nteaching and research. Through a global community of alumni, philanthropists\nand supporters, the Development Office secures the philanthropic investment\nthat enables St Andrews to transform lives through education, research and\ninnovation. We are seeking an experienced and strategic\nleader to join the Development Office as Head of Development Services and\nDeputy Director. This is a pivotal senior leadership role responsible for the leadership\nand management of the Development Services team. The Development Services Team\nincludes collective giving, donor participation and supporter pipeline\ndevelopment, database management and analytics, gift operations, and prospect\nresearch. As a key member of the Development Senior Management Team, you will\nprovide strategic direction for Development Services, deputise for the Director\nof Development, and help shape the future of philanthropy and supporter\nengagement at one of the world's leading universities. The successful candidate will play a central\nrole in supporting the delivery of Making Waves: The Campaign for St Andrews,\nthe University's £300 million fundraising campaign, ensuring the operational\ninfrastructure, data, systems and insight required to support fundraising\nsuccess are effective, robust and future-focused, while providing strategic\nleadership for collective giving and donor participation activity that helps\nbuild the University's future pipeline of philanthropic support. We are looking\nfor a collaborative and forward-thinking leader with significant experience in\ndevelopment services, fundraising operations or a comparable professional\nservices environment. Based at Walter Bower House, Eden Campus,\nGuardbridge, this is an exciting opportunity to make a significant contribution\nto the University's future fundraising success and long-term philanthropic\nambitions. For an informal discussion about the role,\nplease contact Louise Taylor, Head of Development Services at\nlft@st-andrews.ac.uk St Andrews offers more than just a place to work it is\na place to belong. We value collegiality, inclusion, and wellbeing, and we are\ncommitted to creating a workplace where staff can thrive and perform at their\nbest. In addition to the salary on offer for this position,\nthere are a wide range of benefits for staff working at the University of St\nAndrews. The package for the Head of Development Services and Deputy Director\nincludes: Financial contribution to relocation (subject\n    to eligibility) Membership of the USS Pension Scheme with generous\n    employer contributions of 14.5% A hybrid working environment, including partial\n    homeworking where appropriate and a range of family friendly policies,\n    supporting work-life balance Staff discount scheme for local and national goods and\n    services Free staff parking, employee Carshare and Cycle to\n    Work Schemes and subsidised local bus travel Subsidised sports membership, reduced tuition fees on\n    degree programmes for staff, access to training and development opportunities\n    including LinkedIn Learning, access to library facilities, salary sacrifice\n    scheme 34 Days Annual Leave plus 5 Public Holidays. At St Andrews, equality,\ndiversity, and inclusion are central to who we are and form a core pillar of\nour University Strategy. We are committed to creating a fair, inclusive and\nsupportive workplace, reflected in our participation in national diversity charters\nand awards, including Athena Swan, Carer Positive and the Race Equality\nCharter. We particularly welcome\napplications from people from Black, Asian, minority ethnic and minority\nreligions backgrounds and from LGBTQ+ and disabled people. Closing Date: 24 November 2026 Interview dates: 15/16 December 2026 Please quote ref: AD2928LS Job Description: AD2928LSFPs.pdf Development Salary:  £59,967 - £67,469 per annum Start Date: 01 March 2027 or as soon as possible thereafter Apply now Back to search results Head of Development Services and Deputy Director - AD2928 School/Unit: Development Office Posted: 26/10/2026 Closing date: 24/11/2026 Closing time: 23:59 (GMT) Apply now Save Share Login Register Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Password: Sign in Forgot password? Your password has expired, please create a new password below. Your email address has not been verified. Please check your email or click here to resend. Verification email has been resent. Email Address: Please enter a valid email address. Reset password Cancel Email Address: New Password: At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm Password: Update Password Your login attempt was not successful. Please try again Please select Dr Miss Mr Mrs Ms Other Professor Reverend Reverend DR Sir Dr. des. Assistant Professor Mx Title * First name * Last name * Email address * Password * At least 8 characters Uppercase Lowercase Symbols Numbers Confirm password * I have read and understood the terms and conditions I have read and understood the data protection statement Create Account Cancel An email has been sent to your email address. Please confirm that your email address is active by clicking the link in the email. Powered by engage|ats Havas People a Havas Company This site is protected by reCAPTCHA. Contact Us - Application Query Terms and Conditions About Privacy Policy Cookies Accessibility FAQs"
